  "source": "John Fedorco",
  "notes": "Went to USA with father in 1912. Married George Simcoe who was in railroad. George went to saloon a lot. Ann had operation in 1935 and Uncle Johnny provided blood for her as he had the right type. A German doctor stabbed her as she was bloated. She died 3 years later after a visit to Czechoslovakia.",
